# ---------------------------------
#   ports/groups — sets of native applications installed in one step
# ---------------------------------
#
#   group <id> <title>
#   <port>...
#
# A group is its `group` line and the ports named after it, any number to a
# line, up to the next group. `kdos update install <id>` installs each member
# as the port it is, prebuilt from the release's binhost unless --source
# says otherwise, and the installer offers every group by its title. A member
# may be a meta port (kde-gear-games), which installs what it names. The
# image stages this file at /ports/groups, which is where a machine reads it.
#
# An id is a port-name word that is no port's name; a member must be a port.
# script/lib/imageset.py --check, which preflight runs, refuses either. A
# line starting with '#' and a blank line are skipped.

